{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nconst int MAXN = 10;\n\nint mat[MAXN][MAXN];\n\ninline int add(int a, int b) {\n    a += b;\n    return a >= MOD ? a - MOD : a;\n}\n\ninline int sub(int a, int b) {\n    a -= b;\n    return a < 0 ? a + MOD : a;\n}\n\ninline int mul(int a, int b) {\n    return (long long)a * b % MOD;\n}\n\nint powmod(int a, int e) {\n    int res = 1;\n    while (e) {\n        if (e & 1) res = mul(res, a);\n        a = mul(a, a);\n        e >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint inv(int x) {\n    return powmod(x, MOD - 2);\n}\n\nint divide(int a, int b) {\n    return mul(a, inv(b));\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i][j]);\n            mat[i][j] = divide(mat[i][j], 100);\n        }\n\n    vector<pair<vector<int>, int>> cur, nxt;\n    cur.push_back({{0}, 1});\n\n    for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\n        nxt.clear();\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); ++mask) {\n            int prob = 1;\n            for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\n                if (mask & (1 << row))\n                    prob = mul(prob, mat[row][col]);\n                else\n                    prob = mul(prob, sub(1, mat[row][col]));\n            }\n            for (auto &p : cur) {\n                vector<int> tmp;\n                for (int m : p.first) {\n                    int diff = (~m) & mask;\n                    while (diff) {\n                        int low = diff & -diff;\n                        tmp.push_back(m | low);\n                        diff ^= low;\n                    }\n                }\n                if (tmp.empty()) continue;\n                sort(tmp.begin(), tmp.end());\n                tmp.erase(unique(tmp.begin(), tmp.end()), tmp.end());\n                nxt.push_back({tmp, mul(p.second, prob)});\n            }\n        }\n        sort(nxt.begin(), nxt.end());\n        cur.clear();\n        int i = 0;\n        while (i < (int)nxt.size()) {\n            int j = i;\n            int sum = 0;\n            while (j < (int)nxt.size() && nxt[j].first == nxt[i].first) {\n                sum = add(sum, nxt[j].second);\n                ++j;\n            }\n            cur.push_back({nxt[i].first, sum});\n            i = j;\n        }\n    }\n\n    int ans = 0;\n    for (auto &p : cur)\n        ans = add(ans, p.second);\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", ans);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final int MOD = 1000000007;\n    static final int MAXN = 10;\n    static int[][] mat = new int[MAXN][MAXN];\n\n    static int add(int a, int b) {\n        a += b;\n        return a >= MOD ? a - MOD : a;\n    }\n\n    static int sub(int a, int b) {\n        a -= b;\n        return a < 0 ? a + MOD : a;\n    }\n\n    static int mul(int a, int b) {\n        return (int)((long)a * b % MOD);\n    }\n\n    static int powmod(int a, int e) {\n        int res = 1;\n        while (e > 0) {\n            if ((e & 1) == 1) res = mul(res, a);\n            a = mul(a, a);\n            e >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    static int inv(int x) {\n        return powmod(x, MOD - 2);\n    }\n\n    static int divide(int a, int b) {\n        return mul(a, inv(b));\n    }\n\n    static class State {\n        List<Integer> masks;\n        int prob;\n        State(List<Integer> masks, int prob) {\n            this.masks = masks;\n            this.prob = prob;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int inv100 = inv(100);\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n                int val = sc.nextInt();\n                mat[i][j] = divide(val, 100);\n            }\n        }\n\n        List<State> cur = new ArrayList<>();\n        cur.add(new State(new ArrayList<>(Arrays.asList(0)), 1));\n\n        for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\n            List<State> nxt = new ArrayList<>();\n            for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); ++mask) {\n                int prob = 1;\n                for (int row = 0; row < n; ++row) {\n                    if ((mask & (1 << row)) != 0)\n                        prob = mul(prob, mat[row][col]);\n                    else\n                        prob = mul(prob, sub(1, mat[row][col]));\n                }\n                for (State p : cur) {\n                    List<Integer> tmp = new ArrayList<>();\n                    for (int m : p.masks) {\n                        int diff = mask & (~m);\n                        while (diff != 0) {\n                            int low = diff & -diff;\n                            tmp.add(m | low);\n                            diff ^= low;\n                        }\n                    }\n                    if (tmp.isEmpty()) continue;\n                    Collections.sort(tmp);\n                    // remove duplicates\n                    List<Integer> unique = new ArrayList<>();\n                    for (int i = 0; i < tmp.size(); ++i) {\n                        if (i == 0 || !tmp.get(i).equals(tmp.get(i-1)))\n                            unique.add(tmp.get(i));\n                    }\n                    nxt.add(new State(unique, mul(p.prob, prob)));\n                }\n            }\n            // sort nxt by masks list\n            Collections.sort(nxt, new Comparator<State>() {\n                public int compare(State a, State b) {\n                    List<Integer> la = a.masks;\n                    List<Integer> lb = b.masks;\n                    int minLen = Math.min(la.size(), lb.size());\n                    for (int i = 0; i < minLen; ++i) {\n                        int cmp = la.get(i).compareTo(lb.get(i));\n                        if (cmp != 0) return cmp;\n                    }\n                    return Integer.compare(la.size(), lb.size());\n                }\n            });\n            cur.clear();\n            int i = 0;\n            while (i < nxt.size()) {\n                int j = i;\n                int sum = 0;\n                while (j < nxt.size() && nxt.get(j).masks.equals(nxt.get(i).masks)) {\n                    sum = add(sum, nxt.get(j).prob);\n                    ++j;\n                }\n                cur.add(new State(nxt.get(i).masks, sum));\n                i = j;\n            }\n        }\n\n        int ans = 0;\n        for (State p : cur)\n            ans = add(ans, p.prob);\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -3.4689302992774174e-05, -5.8412379075889476e-06, 0.0, -1.6331539882230572e-05, -0.006998075637966394, -1.3828182090946939e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.001050635357387364, -0.001503766